=== VERDICT (REFUTE lens) 2026-11-08 16:17:03 -0500 ===
Mechanism: CONFIRMED. GNU Make 3.81 hands '$$' to the shell as one '$' in both $(shell) and recipe context (arms A, C);
  '$$$$' is what yields a PID (arms B, D) -- so the probe can distinguish the two and the reproducer's sh model was right.
  cpp/Makefile sha256 c89066a2... matches the README; lines 45 and 49 carry the token; not stale.
Documented? NO. OC-121 Item 5 (ORCHESTRATOR-CHECKS.md, commit b53ff5d) and the Makefile comment block describe the probe,
  not its temp path. NOTICE, FORK-DIVERGENCE-AND-TRUST.md and FINDINGS-TRACKER.md are silent on it.
Reachability: build-time only; needs neither EA_ALLOW_SHORT_DATASET nor a short dataset; no effect on any estimator figure.
  Preconditions for harm (a hostile co-tenant on the build host, or two make processes inside the ~100 ms probe window) are
  absent in the known deployments: a single-developer Mac, and single-tenant GitHub runners that run make SEQUENTIALLY
  (x86-64-platform-facts.yml lines 113-130).
Consequence chain as written is WRONG on this compiler: a non-compiling plant does NOT flip FLOAT_STORE (grep MATCHES the
  driver warning for garbage and for a directory alike -> FLOAT_STORE stays ""). The measured effect of a plant is on the
  SECOND probe: IGNORED_FLAG_IS_ERROR becomes "" and the -Werror guard OC-121 added is silently dropped. No denial of build.
  Worse-than-stated branch, NOT exercised: macOS has no fs.protected_symlinks, so a planted symlink would make the probe's
  printf overwrite the symlink's target as the builder; still requires a hostile local user.
Severity stays LOW, direction neutral. cli-build.md:273 carries the same unmeasured denial-of-build chain; correct both.
